y can figure out order because  obviously when they film a movie they  never actually film it in the order it's  like written you know they'll do this  but they could they could film the first  bit of the movie at the right very end  and  vice versa it depends on when actors are  available when production sets are  available and all this sort of thing and  having a storyboard is is very useful  for that you can actually physically  take it apart and put it back together  again and it allows you to see the movie  in a very visual way  so have the storyboards been created  for the executives to get an idea while  they're trying to decide whether they're  going to produce these three movies or  not or is it actually further along than  that and they're designing and creating  the storyboard so they can start  thinking about cost and creative  schedules and all this sort of thing  well  genuinely if they are going to produce  this i think it will be because jeff  bezos has basically said yeah go on  let's do it  how much they spend on it is going to be  the important part here they are not  going to spend hundreds of millions of  pounds produced in these three movies it  is going to be more like a tv sort of  level of um production value i could see  that the basically the budget being  roughly similar to what the season six  budget was and they only produced six  episodes for that series don't forget  but if we get that sort of budget for  each movie we can get something that is  visually spectacular and don't forget  they can continue to use a lot of the  sets and props and things a lot of the  money to produce this series might have  actually already been spent  so you can  use a lot and save money in lots of  different ways by using the props etc  from the series  and we're going to want them to do that  as well because we want them to continue  the look of the show now my source  doesn't know what stage this is at all  he can tell me is that the storyboards  exist 